## App Review Notes

Verdure is a native iOS document and image utility app.

The core functionality can be tested without creating an account or signing in.

To test the main workflow:

1. Open the app and select "Scan Document" to launch the document scanning experience.
2. Scan one or more document pages.
3. Review the scanned pages and create a multi-page PDF.
4. Use "Adjust" to apply image filters, rotate, mirror, resize, or change JPEG compression quality.
5. Use "Convert" to export an image as PNG, JPEG, or PDF.
6. Open "PDF Studio" to combine multiple images/pages into a multi-page PDF.
7. Test A4/US Letter sizing, portrait/landscape orientation, and the optional watermark.
8. Use the system share sheet to export or share the resulting file.

Verdure's file-processing functionality is designed to operate on-device. No account is required for the core scanning, conversion, image adjustment, compression, or PDF creation workflows.

Camera access is used only to launch the built-in document scanner (VisionKit) so the user can capture physical documents. Photo library access is used only to import the specific photo the user selects via Apple's PhotosPicker — the app does not browse or access the rest of the photo library.

